"""southern_barrens: speeches for the story pass, and places named where the old accept line used to carry them."""

STORY = {
    'ratchet_raptor_hides': ("I'm Fishmonger Gribble. Yes, I know what the stall says, but hear me out. I've got a side trade in raptor hide.\n\nFish is the business. Fish is reliable and boring, and it's kept this stall open through two bad years. Raptor hide is the margin, and the Sunscale raptors are the closest real supply on this coast. Everything else comes up from the south at a price that eats the point of it.\n\nThe Sunscale screechers hunt thickest along the Southfury banks, north of here, and the lashtails keep to the Raptor Grounds in the Southern Barrens. Bring the hides back as whole as you can manage. That isn't fussiness. A hide with a hole through the middle is worth about a third, because the buyers cut panels, and a panel has to be clean.", 'Skin them along the belly. A cut down the back ruins the best panel.'),
    'ratchet_thinning_the_grounds': ("I'm Kala, and I hunt for the camp. Walk with me a moment.\n\nThe kodo moved south early this year, and I've been finding out why. It's the raptors. The Sunscale on the Raptor Grounds have bred past what the ground can feed, and the lashtails, the young bold hunters, have started running the herds instead of the strays. A herd that's run doesn't graze, and a herd that doesn't graze doesn't calve. I won't have this camp go hungry in spring for the sake of a raptor's good year.\n\nThin the Sunscale Lashtails on the Raptor Grounds, south through Camp Taurajo on the east side of the Southern Barrens. Don't kill them all, because the Grounds are theirs. Kill only enough that they remember it.", 'Leave the nesting females be. The Grounds need the next generation, just a smaller one.'),
    'taurajo_word_from_bael_modan': ("The dwarves have been digging at Bael Modan for years, and nobody here has minded very much. I want to be fair about that. They put a hole in some ground nobody was grazing, and for a long while that was the whole story.\n\nWord now is they've built a proper fortress over it, Bael'dun Keep, and that's a different thing. You don't build a keep over a hole unless you mean to be at the bottom of it for a very long time, or unless you expect somebody to come and stop you.\n\nI'm meant to be watching the centaur, so go south to Bael Modan and look at the keep for me before Camp Taurajo turns its attention south. I'd rather look foolish for asking than find out from a dwarf.", None),
    'org_razormane_incursion': ("The ridge is confirmed, so now we bleed it, and I'll be straight about the goal. It isn't conquest and it never was. I want the Razormane to think again about testing us.\n\nI'm not taking that ridge. I haven't got the men, and I couldn't hold it if I had. What I want is for the next quilboar who suggests pushing toward the southern trade routes to get an argument from somebody in his own camp, and that only happens if this raid costs them. A small raid they shrug off. A real one gets talked about round their own fire.\n\nThe Razormane Stalkers work Blackthorn Ridge, north of Razorfen Kraul. Kill as many as you can, as obviously as you can.", None),
    'org_the_broodkeeper': ("The outer tunnels are confirmed dangerous, which I expected, and organised, which I didn't. There's a Broodkeeper deeper in the Broodspiral, south-east of Ratchet, a caster of sorts, tending the egg chambers.\n\nTending is the word I keep coming back to, and it's why I'm sending you instead of writing another report. Silithid don't tend. They lay and they leave, and the hive works or it doesn't. Every text I own agrees on that. Something down below is looking after eggs on purpose, and the growth we've measured is exactly what you'd expect if it were.\n\nEvery day it lives, the hive grows faster. Kill it and buy the surface some real time. That's all I'm promising, because the eggs are already laid.", None),
}
